    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Description</h2><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3006440/extras/5c8d086720572d8f725b23e8c534630f.avif?t=1716637432\" width=184 height=102 /></span><br><br>Following a bizarre incident, you find yourself trapped in a barely habitable world of floating continents. You're not the first to end up here - over the centuries, hundreds of other people have been transported into Aeronesia as well with nothing more than the items they had on them at the time. And in a world without food, equipment, and law... those other people may be more of a threat than any other danger you might face.<br><br>You're not trying to save this world, you're trying to <i>leave</i> it.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Main Features</h2><br>Aeronesia is a non-linear platform RPG with heavy emphasis on:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Exploration, player freedom, and worldbuilding<br></li><li> Quest-based progression, with the player deciding whether and how to approach the tasks they're given<br></li><li> Combat featuring melee weapons and firearms, as well as traps and thrown items<br></li><li> Character customization through equipment and perks<br></li><li> Dialogue with varying outcomes and a choice of factions to work for or against<br></li><li> Factions, locations and phenomena whose history and nature you discover over time<br></li><li> Detailed pixel art graphics and animations<br></li><li> Dark humour</li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Description</h2><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3006440/extras/5c8d086720572d8f725b23e8c534630f.avif?t=1716637432\" width=184 height=102 /></span><br><br>Following a bizarre incident, you find yourself trapped in a barely habitable world of floating continents. You're not the first to end up here - over the centuries, hundreds of other people have been transported into Aeronesia as well with nothing more than the items they had on them at the time. And in a world without food, equipment, and law... those other people may be more of a threat than any other danger you might face.<br><br>You're not trying to save this world, you're trying to <i>leave</i> it.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Main Features</h2><br>Aeronesia is a non-linear platform RPG with heavy emphasis on:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Exploration, player freedom, and worldbuilding<br></li><li> Quest-based progression, with the player deciding whether and how to approach the tasks they're given<br></li><li> Combat featuring melee weapons and firearms, as well as traps and thrown items<br></li><li> Character customization through equipment and perks<br></li><li> Dialogue with varying outcomes and a choice of factions to work for or against<br></li><li> Factions, locations and phenomena whose history and nature you discover over time<br></li><li> Detailed pixel art graphics and animations<br></li><li> Dark humour</li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Aeronesia is a non-linear platform RPG with emphasis on exploration, combat, dialogue and quest-based progression. After an accident transports you and hundreds of other people into an alien world, it's up to you to find a way to survive and discover some means of getting back home.",
